  "brief": "Fox has completed its $22 billion acquisition of streaming giant Roku, with the deal expected to bring $400 million in cost synergies.\n\nFox / Roku (Completed): Fox Acquires Roku. Fox has acquired streaming giant Roku in a $22 billion deal [1, 2, 3]. The acquisition is now complete, with Fox owning Roku [4, 5, 6]. The deal is expected to bring $400 million in cost synergies [7]. The streaming platform will remain an open ecosystem [8].\nShield AI / Echodyne (Announced): Shield AI and Echodyne Deal. Shield AI is buying Echodyne, a Bill Gates-backed radar maker [13, 14]. The deal is valued at $5.3 billion [13, 14]. Shield AI will raise $2.5 billion at a $28.8 billion valuation [14].\nAlfa Laval / NAVTOR (Announced): Alfa Laval to Acquire NAVTOR. Alfa Laval is acquiring NAVTOR for $700 million [15, 16]. The deal was announced on November 6 [15, 16]. No further information is available [15, 16].\nThe New York Times / Letterboxd (Rumored): The New York Times May Acquire Letterboxd. The New York Times is in advanced talks to acquire film social network Letterboxd [17, 18, 19]. The deal is valued at $330 million [17, 18, 19]. No further details have been disclosed [17, 18, 19].\nSilver Lake and PIF / Unity (Rumored): Silver Lake and PIF in Unity Talks. Silver Lake and PIF are in talks to buy gaming software provider Unity [21, 22, 24]. The deal is rumored to be worth around $25 billion [22, 25]. No further information is available at this time [26].\nAdani Ports / Evos (Announced): Adani Ports to Acquire Evos. Adani Ports is acquiring Evos in a €2.56 billion deal [27, 28, 29]. The deal aims to expand Adani Ports' European liquid storage footprint [27, 28, 29]. No further details on the deal's next steps have been announced [27, 28, 29].\nAkzoNobel / Axalta (Pending approval): AkzoNobel and Axalta Merger. AkzoNobel and Axalta have secured EU antitrust approval for their $25B merger deal [30, 31]. Regulators are seeking two asset sales as part of the merger deal [31]. The companies have proposed remedies for EU approval of the merger deal [32]. The merger is nearing approval in both the US and EU after unit sales [35].\nAlif / Analog Devices (Completed): Analog Devices Completes Alif Deal. Analog Devices has completed its acquisition of Alif [36]. The deal expands Analog Devices' edge AI capabilities [36].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Salesforce Buys Cresta, CrowdStrike Acquires Two AI Companies, Out West Restaurant Group B [37].\n- Apollo’s Brightspeed in Creditor Talks for Billions in New Money [38].\n- EXCLUSIVE: Networking firm Extreme Networks explores sale, sources say [42].",
